==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Indo-European|kuH-t-|lang=la}}, [[zero-grade]] without [[s-mobile]] form of {{proto|Indo-European|(s)kewH-|to cover|title=|lang=la}}. Cognates include Welsh {{term|cwd||scrotum|lang=cy}}, Lithuanian {{term|kutys|kutỹs|purse|lang=lt}} and Old English {{term|hyd|hȳd|lang=ang}} (English {{term|hide|lang=en}}). Related to {{term|obscurus|obscūrus|dark, obscure|lang=la}} and {{term|culus||bottom|lang=la}}.

